 - **Only the server decides:** the client's pick is bounded by the stored best when the lobby stores it, and the game place plays the stored choice, never what the client sent.
 - **(prep)**, the user may veto any: a new run after game over starts on the same level again (the game place returns players to the lobby after a game over, so this matters only where a run is restarted in place); the arrows work by click and tap, by the controller's selection (as START does), and by the Left and Right arrow keys, bound above the camera's own use of them; the best is raised each time a run reaches a new level (not only at game over); the game place claims the stored choice once, so a later arrival without a new pick starts on level 1, unless the lobby's write (which the teleport waits for at most 5 s) landed after that claim, in which case the next arrival starts on the late choice; a store that fails or does not answer within 10 s starts the run on level 1, and a lobby that cannot read the best shows no picker; the picker's best is read once when the player arrives in the lobby.
 
